Liquid Neon wallpapers — PNG originals
======================================

The 42 PNGs behind this pack are owner-authored: Skyy generated them himself
with an AI image generator and supplied them to engineering on 2026-09-09.
Wholly owned, no stock-library licence, no third-party rights holder, no
attribution requirement. Confirmed by Skyy on 2026-09-09 (SKY-11591).

The canonical licence record — the one that covers redistribution inside the
installer — is kept next to the assets that actually ship:

    frontend/src/assets/wallpapers/LICENSE

Keep that file authoritative and this one a pointer, so the two cannot drift.

The originals are NOT in this repository
----------------------------------------
The PNGs total 68.2 MB and would live in git history forever. Ivy ruled on
2026-09-09 (SKY-11675) that they must not enter it. `originals/` is git-ignored;
the owner holds the files and is regenerating them at higher resolution
(SKY-11600). They are also never packaged: `electron-builder.json` sets
`files: ["out/**/*", "package.json"]`, so only what the renderer build emits
reaches the installer, and this directory sits outside that tree by
construction.

`PROVENANCE.json` next to this file is what replaces the blobs. It records, per
original: the staged filename, pixel dimensions, byte size, a SHA-256 of the
bytes, the owner's folder and filename, and which shipped WebP was cropped from
it — or why it was rejected. A restaged copy can therefore be proven identical
to the file a given wallpaper was actually made from.

To rebuild: restage the PNGs under `originals/<setKey>/<setKey>-src-NN.png`,
check each SHA-256 against `PROVENANCE.json`, then run the build. See
docs/design/wallpaper-pipeline.md.
